---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import { inlineLinks } from '../lib/text';
import { socials, raceDay } from '../site';

const education = (await getCollection('education')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const daysToRace = Math.ceil((raceDay.valueOf() - Date.now()) / 86_400_000);
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Mathematician, actuary, former researcher and software engineer. Curious about far too many things, and training for a half Ironman."
  image="/images/IMG_0513.JPG"
>
  <section class="section section--flush intro">
    <div class="wrap intro__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="label">About</p>
        <h1 class="display intro__title">Hi — I'm Erik.</h1>
        <div class="lede intro__lede">
          <p>
            I studied maths, spent three years doing physics research, worked as a software engineer
            for a while, and now I'm an actuary. From the outside that probably looks like I couldn't
            make my mind up. From the inside it's been the same question the whole way through: how
            do you deal with things you can't predict?
          </p>
          <p>
            These days I work in insurance, where the maths I learned for quantum systems turns out
            to be uncomfortably good at describing claims. From September I'm also doing an MSc in
            Actuarial Science and Financial Engineering at KU Leuven, mostly to put proper names to
            things I'd been doing by instinct.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="portrait">
        <img src="/images/IMG_0513.JPG" alt="Erik Pillon" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="comment">off-season, palm trees, no watch. it does happen.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="01" title="The curious part" />
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="prose prose--tight">
          <p>
            I've never been good at having one interest. Right now the list includes how insurers
            set reserves, the history of science, Formula 1 data, index funds, note-taking systems,
            and how to swim in a straight line in open water. They take turns, but none of them
            really go away.
          </p>
          <p>
            Which means my side projects follow whatever I'm into at the time. A personal finance
            app because I wanted an honest look at where my money actually is. A second brain
            because ideas never turn up when I'm ready for them. A pub quiz scoring app because
            keeping score on napkins is a solved problem and I'd been solving it badly for years.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose--tight">
          <p>
            The one thing that has stuck is <strong>talking about science</strong>. It started
            during my research years, when I ran{' '}
            <a class="link" href="https://luxdoc.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LuxDoc</a>,
            the University of Luxembourg's doctoral students' association, and spent more evenings
            than I can count putting on Science Slams and Three Minute Thesis contests.
          </p>
          <p>
            These days it's{' '}
            <a class="link" href="https://scientificchronicles.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Scientific Chronicles
            </a>, a newsletter about the people and the dates behind the
            discoveries, plus an archive of scientific anniversaries that goes with it. I read a lot
            and can't stop taking notes; a fair amount of that ends up{' '}
            <a class="link" href="/writing">here</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="02" title="Off the clock" />
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat__value">1:30:37</p>
          <p class="stat__key">half-marathon PB</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat__value">70.3</p>
          <p class="stat__key">first half Ironman, 20 Sep 2026</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat__value">{daysToRace > 0 ? daysToRace : 0}</p>
          <p class="stat__key">days to go</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <p class="stat__value">3</p>
          <p class="stat__key">sports, one of which I can actually do</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="lede stats__note">
        I'm a competitive triathlete in the sense that I turn up and race, and a
        triathlete-in-training in the sense that the swim is still an argument I'm losing. Training
        is the one part of my week I don't try to optimise, which is probably why I like it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="03" title="Where I studied" />
      <ol class="timeline">
        {
          education.map((entry) => (
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <div class="timeline__when">
                <span class="mono">{entry.data.dates}</span>
                {entry.data.current && <span class="status" data-status="wip">current</span>}
              </div>
              <div class="timeline__what">
                <h3 class="timeline__qual">{entry.data.qualification}</h3>
                <p class="timeline__place">{entry.data.name}</p>
                <p class="timeline__desc" set:html={inlineLinks(entry.data.description)} />
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="comment timeline__note">
        what the research was actually about, in plain words:{' '}
        <a class="link" href="/forum_EP.pdf">a short introduction (PDF)</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="04" title="Say hello" />
      <p class="lede contact__lede">
        Happy to talk about insurance maths, running, note-taking systems, or why your favourite
        economics model is wrong. Email is the surest way to reach me.
      </p>
      <ul class="contact">
        {
          socials.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a
                class="contact__link"
                href={s.href}
                target={s.href.startsWith('mailto:') ? undefined : '_blank'}
                rel={s.href.startsWith('mailto:') ? undefined : 'me noopener'}
              >
                <span class="contact__label">{s.label}</span>
                <span class="contact__handle mono">{s.handle}</span>
                <span class="contact__go" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .intro__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(14rem, 0.8fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .intro__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.2rem);
    margin: 1.1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .intro__lede p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .portrait {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    filter: saturate(0.9);
  }

  .portrait figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .prose--tight {
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .prose--tight > * + * {
    margin-top: 1.1em;
  }

  /* stats strip */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 11rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .stat {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .stat__value {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.35rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat__key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .stats__note {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  /* education timeline */
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .timeline__item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 1.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .timeline__when {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .timeline__qual {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .timeline__place {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .timeline__desc {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 62ch;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .timeline__note {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* contact */
  .contact__lede {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .contact {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .contact__link {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem minmax(0, 1fr) 1.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.95rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact__link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .contact__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact__link:hover .contact__label {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .contact__handle {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .contact__go {
    justify-self: end;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact__link:hover .contact__go {
    color: var(--accent);
    transform: translate(2px, -2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .intro__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .portrait {
      max-width: 20rem;
      order: -1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .timeline__item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .timeline__when {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .contact__link {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5rem;
      gap: 0.2rem 1rem;
    }

    .contact__go {
      grid-row: 1 / span 2;
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
